	"name": "Gunfighter's Stance",
	"type": "feature",
	"img": "icons/equipment/feet/boots-collared-rounded-leather.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>At 11th level, you position your body relative to attackers in ways that reduce their chances of hitting. Not just facing them side-on to present the narrowest target line, but you can often predict where a bullet will go. If you are hit by a ranged weapon attack you may expend your reaction to reduce the damage by 1d10 + your Dexterity modifier + your Adept Level. You may then make an immediate attack roll on the target with a light firearm you possess, even if the firearm is not readied.</p><p>In addition, possessing this ability counts as having the @UUID[Compendium.a5e.a5e-class-features.Item.6hkqh73swnupa2r7]{Deflect Missiles} focus feature.</p>",
